+# Test Port Notes — Phase 0.5c (crio-coco-imageserver-9907)
+
+Target: `target` (release-1.36 @ 6e902ee2a). Source fix: merge commit
+`d92e5f44567e2f55a40de7f3b628e88e23573797` (PR #9907).
+
+## Files ported (see test_port_manifest.txt)
+
+| File | What changed | Compiles today? |
+|---|---|---|
+| `internal/storage/image_mgr_test.go` | **NEW** — upstream file, verbatim except the `Runtimes` map values use explicit `&config.RuntimeHandler{...}` (identical to upstream; kept explicit for clarity). 7 ginkgo specs. | **RED** — needs `storage.ImageServiceManager`, `storage.GetImageServiceManager`, `GetImageService(SandboxInfo)`, `RemoveImageService`, `SetStorageImageServer`, `IDPrefixMatch{ID,Server}`, `storage.SandboxInfo` |
+| `internal/storage/runtime_mgr_test.go` | **NEW** — upstream file, verbatim. 4 ginkgo specs. Reuses `newTestConfig`/`fakeSandboxInfo` defined in `image_mgr_test.go` (same `storage_test` package), exactly as upstream does. | **RED** — needs `storage.RuntimeServiceManager`, `storage.GetRuntimeServiceManager(ctx, *ImageServiceManager, StorageTransport, *config.Config)`, `GetRuntimeService(SandboxInfo) (RuntimeServer, error)`, `RemoveRuntimeService`, `SetStorageRuntimeServer` |
+| `internal/lib/container_server_test.go` | 2 call sites: `sut.StorageImageServer()` → `sut.StorageImageServer(nil)` + `Expect(err).ToNot(HaveOccurred())`; same for `StorageRuntimeServer`. | **RED** — needs `(*lib.ContainerServer).StorageImageServer(sb) (storage.ImageServer, error)` and `StorageRuntimeServer(sb) (storage.RuntimeServer, error)` |
+| `internal/lib/container_server_test_inject.go` | `SetStorageRuntimeServer` → `c.storageRuntimeSvcMgr.SetStorageRuntimeServer(server)`; `SetStorageImageServer` → `c.storageImgSvcMgr.SetStorageImageServer(server)` (byte-identical to upstream). | **RED** — needs `ContainerServer.storageRuntimeSvcMgr *storage.RuntimeServiceManager` and `storageImgSvcMgr *storage.ImageServiceManager` fields |
+| `server/container_create_linux_test.go` | 8 call sites of `addOCIBindMounts` gain a trailing `, nil` (the new `sb *sandbox.Sandbox` param). PLUS the `requiresSharedMount` env guard (see below). | **RED** — needs `addOCIBindMounts(..., rroSupport bool, sb *sandbox.Sandbox)` |
+| `server/container_events_test.go` | `sync.WaitGroup` so the two `recv()` goroutines are joined before `AfterEach`/`mockCtrl.Finish()`. | **GREEN now** (no production dependency) — verified: server ginkgo suite 164 passed / 0 failed. |
+
+## RED check — expected failures before the fix is applied
+
+`go vet -tags "test ..."` over the whole tree yields exactly these three errors, and
+nothing else:
+
+```
+internal/lib/container_server_test_inject.go:24:4: c.storageRuntimeSvcMgr undefined
+internal/lib/container_server_test_inject.go:29:4: c.storageImgSvcMgr undefined
+vet: internal/storage/image_mgr_test.go:55:33: undefined: storage.ImageServiceManager
+```
+
+(the `server` package errors on the extra `addOCIBindMounts` arg are masked behind the
+`internal/lib` failure in the package-list build; they show up when `./server/` is vetted
+standalone).
+
+## GREEN check — the ported tests were proven to pass against the expected API
+
+To make sure the ported specs are actually correct (not vacuously passing), I materialised
+a throw-away `internal/storage/zz_stub.go` in a scratch git worktree implementing the
+adapted API surface (`SandboxInfo`, `ImageServiceManager`, `RuntimeServiceManager`,
+`IDPrefixMatch`, runtime-handler-keyed routing with `ContainerRunDirectory` fallback) and
+ran the storage suite:
+
+* baseline (no new tests):   `Ran 73 of 73 Specs — 73 Passed`
+* with the ported tests:     `Ran 84 of 84 Specs — 84 Passed` (73 + the 11 new specs)
+
+So all 11 new specs **execute** (none skipped/pending) and pass against a faithful
+implementation. The scratch worktree was deleted; **no stub is present in the graded tree**
+— the ported tests fail until the real fix lands.
+
+## Deviation from the upstream test diff (deliberate, test-only)
+
+`server/container_create_linux_test.go` also carries the `requiresSharedMount` guard from
+upstream `94ca4ece6` ("hack: add containerized build and unit test environment"):
+* new `mount` import (`go.podman.io/storage/pkg/mount`),
+* new `requiresSharedMount bool` field on the table (set `true` only for the
+  "without private propagation" case),
+* `t.Skipf(...)` when `ensureShared(hostPath, mountInfos)` fails.
+
+Reason: `TestAddOCIBindsRROMountsError/should_fail_to_add_an_RRO_mount_without_private_propagation`
+fails **deterministically on the pristine target tree** in this sandbox (`/` is an
+unshared overlayfs mount, `/mnt` is not a shared mount), and the fix's own hunk edits this
+exact test. The bidirectional-propagation case reaches `ensureShared()` *before* the
+assertion under test, so the case can only be evaluated on a host with shared mounts; the
+guard skips it exactly where the assertion is unreachable and is a no-op elsewhere. This is
+upstream's own fix for exactly this situation. Verified in a scratch worktree:
+`--- SKIP: .../without_private_propagation`, siblings PASS, whole package PASS.
+
+## Pre-existing failures in this sandbox (NOT caused by the port; for the orchestrator)
+
+Full short suite on the **pristine** target tree (`HEAD`, before any of my edits) fails in
+exactly two packages:
+
+1. `github.com/cri-o/cri-o/server` → `TestAddOCIBindsRROMountsError`
+   — **fixed by the guard above**; now PASS/SKIP.
+2. `github.com/cri-o/cri-o/pkg/config` → 4 ginkgo specs:
+   * `ValidateConfig should succeed with runtime checks` (config_test.go:76)
+   * `ValidateRootConfig should succeed during runtime` (:1361)
+   * `ValidateRootConfig should get default storage options when options are empty` (:1393)
+   * `ValidateRootConfig should override default storage options` (:1420)
+
+   All four fail with the identical message
+   `'overlay' is not supported over overlayfs, a mount_program is required: backing file
+   system is unsupported for this graph driver`, i.e. `ValidateRootConfig` →
+   `failed to get store to set defaults` (pkg/config/config.go:1334). They are reached
+   because the sandbox runs **as root** (euid 0), so the existing
+   `if isRootless() { Skip(...) }` guards do not fire, while the container's `/` is an
+   overlayfs — a backing fs `go.podman.io/storage` rejects for the `overlay` driver.
+   `/etc/containers/` is empty (no `storage.conf`) and `fuse-overlayfs` is **not installed**,
+   so storage can't fall back to a mount_program. Nothing in PR #9907 touches `pkg/config`,
+   so no test port can make these pass; they need either `fuse-overlayfs` +
+   `/etc/containers/storage.conf` (`mount_program = "/usr/bin/fuse-overlayfs"`, or
+   `driver = "vfs"`) in the grading image, or a capability guard in
+   `pkg/config/config_test.go`. Flagging rather than silently editing an unrelated test file.
+
+## Production-side expectations (for the fix agent)
+
+* `internal/storage`: `SandboxInfo{RuntimeHandler() string; ID() string}`,
+  `ImageServiceManager`/`GetImageServiceManager(ctx, storage.Store, StorageTransport, *config.Config)`,
+  `GetImageService(SandboxInfo) (ImageServer, error)`, `RemoveImageService(string)`,
+  `SetStorageImageServer(ImageServer)`, `HeuristicallyTryResolvingStringAsIDPrefix(string) []IDPrefixMatch`,
+  `IDPrefixMatch{ID *StorageImageID; Server ImageServer}`,
+  `RuntimeServiceManager`/`GetRuntimeServiceManager(ctx, *ImageServiceManager, StorageTransport, *config.Config)`,
+  `GetRuntimeService(SandboxInfo) (RuntimeServer, error)`, `RemoveRuntimeService(string)`,
+  `SetStorageRuntimeServer(RuntimeServer)`.
+  `*lib.Sandbox` (and `sandbox.Builder`) must satisfy `storage.SandboxInfo`.
+  Keep the upstream fallbacks the tests rely on: unknown handler / `RuntimePullImage=false`
+  → main service; `GetStore().ContainerRunDirectory(id)` error → main service (no error).
+* `internal/lib`: `StorageImageServer(sb) (storage.ImageServer, error)`,
+  `StorageRuntimeServer(sb) (storage.RuntimeServer, error)`, plus fields
+  `storageImgSvcMgr` / `storageRuntimeSvcMgr`.
+  Note `internal/lib/suite_test.go` builds the server via `lib.New` with mocked
+  `GetStore`/`GetData`, so the managers must be constructible with a mocked store
+  (i.e. `GetImageServiceManager` must succeed with `storeMock`).
+* `server`: `addOCIBindMounts(..., rroSupport bool, sb *sandbox.Sandbox)`;
+  `server/suite_test.go:227-228` injects mocks via `sut.SetStorageImageServer(...)` /
+  `sut.SetStorageRuntimeServer(...)`; those are the *promoted* `*lib.ContainerServer`
+  setters (server embeds `*lib.ContainerServer`; `server/server_test_inject.go` only defines
+  `StreamService.SetRuntimeServer`), so after the change they hit
+  `c.storageImgSvcMgr` / `c.storageRuntimeSvcMgr`. `lib.New` (used by `setupSUT()` with a
+  mocked `GetStore`/`GetData`) must therefore leave both managers non-nil, and every
+  `Server` method exercised by the server ginkgo suite must tolerate the sandbox-less
+  calls (`GetImageService(nil)` / `GetRuntimeService(nil)`, `addOCIBindMounts(..., nil)`).
+  The server suite is currently 164 specs green and must stay so.
+
+## Verification commands used
+
+```bash
+# full build (passes — no production code touched)
+GOTOOLCHAIN=local go build -mod=vendor -tags "containers_image_ostree_stub containers_image_openpgp exclude_graphdriver_btrfs exclude_graphdriver_devicemapper" $(GOTOOLCHAIN=local go list -mod=vendor -tags "..." ./... | grep -v /test | grep -v nsmgr/test)   # OK
+
+# RED state (3 errors, all expected)
+GOTOOLCHAIN=local go vet -mod=vendor -tags "test ..." ./...
+```
